            <ArticleTitle>Autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome: meticulous care for diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>197</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome (ALPS) is a prototypic disorder of abnormal lymphocyte homeostasis. In the September 2005 issue of The Iranian Journal of Allergy, Asthma and Immunology, a patient with clinical features consistent with ALPS was described. Although the clinical presentation was in favor of ALPS, a precise diagnosis needed more laboratory evaluations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
